\ `parse-json` over objects nested 24 deep, `{"a":{"a":...1...}}`.
\
\ The census reads the deepest point, which is the innermost value, so its middle levels are the
\ per-level path from one `parse-json-value` to the next through the object arm.

use "data/json" ;

\\ `str` concatenated `n` times.
repeat-string: ( str: string n: fixnum -- result: string ) [ "" swap [ over #append ] times nip ] ;

"{\"a\":" 24 repeat-string "1" #append "}" 24 repeat-string #append
parse-json drop
